Q: Discord API: Get Application Name A: <p>I don't think there's a way to do this if without having an authorised user:</p>
<p>If you have a user's token (bot tokens don't work), you can make a request to <code>https://discord.com/api/v9/oauth2/authorize?client_id=xxxxxxxxxxxxx</code></p>
<p>and get a response like</p>
<pre class="lang-json prettyprint-override"><code>{
    &quot;application&quot;: {
        &quot;id&quot;: &quot;&quot;,
        &quot;name&quot;: &quot;Example Application&quot;,
        &quot;icon&quot;: &quot;xxxxx&quot;,
        &quot;description&quot;: &quot;&quot;,
        &quot;summary&quot;: &quot;&quot;,
        &quot;type&quot;: null,
        &quot;is_monetized&quot;: false,
        &quot;is_verified&quot;: false,
        &quot;is_discoverable&quot;: false,
        &quot;cover_image&quot;: &quot;xxxxx&quot;,
        &quot;hook&quot;: true,
        &quot;storefront_available&quot;: false,
        &quot;integration_types_config&quot;: {
            &quot;0&quot;: {}
        },
        &quot;verify_key&quot;: &quot;xxxxx&quot;,
        &quot;flags&quot;: 0,
        &quot;flags_new&quot;: &quot;0&quot;
    },
    &quot;user&quot;: {
        // your user info
    },
    &quot;authorized&quot;: false,
    &quot;integration_type&quot;: 0,
    &quot;redirect_uri&quot;: null
}
</code></pre>
<p>If you use the Discord Rich Presence RPC system, it will also return the application ID with in the name field in the 'SET_ACTIVITY' response</p>
<pre class="lang-json prettyprint-override"><code>{
  cmd: 'SET_ACTIVITY',
  data: {
    details: 'my rich presence',
    state: 'details here',
    name: 'APPLICATION_NAME',
    application_id: 'XXXX',
    platform: 'desktop',
    type: 0,
  },
  evt: null,
  nonce: ''
}
</code></pre>

Q: Regex remove repeated +-*/ characters from a string in javascript A: <p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>console.log('+-111+++22-33*****4//////3'.replace(/([-/*+])\1+/g, '$1'));</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>
<p>Analysis:</p>
<p><code>([-/*+])</code> - capture your target character to replace into a capture group<br />
<code>\1+</code> - match any number of repeating captured character<br />
<code>/g</code> - global replace<br />
<code>$1</code> - replace with 1 captured character</p>
<p>An <code>Array::reduce()</code> one-liner:</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>const str = '+-111+++22-33*****4//////3';

const res = str.split('').reduce((r,c,i,arr) =&gt; i &amp;&amp; arr[i-1] === c &amp;&amp; '*/+-'.includes(c) ? r : r + c, '');

console.log(res);</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>
<p>And a benchmark:</p>
<pre><code>` Chrome/148
-------------------------------------------------------
regexp           ■ 1.00x | x1000000 138 142 143 144 144
Array::reduce()    1.32x | x1000000 182 184 188 188 196
Tim                1.64x | x1000000 226 228 239 239 246
------------------------------------------------------- `
</code></pre>
<p><a href="https://silentmantra.github.io/benchmark#H4sIAAAAAAAACm1RS07DMBS8yhAhbNf5kJZVg%2FmcgA0LpLqL4LqtRXCqFweBaO%2BO3AS1EszCsmbeG43H34lpVzaZJ6b1XUAXCApMZmVZSimn02w2m0TcFEfMWKW99kWBh1frzfa9pjc8u3ft1703wbU%2BWrgd7wS%2BtQeAj5rQ9gEKOtFJdSKbuosse2EjuW6Jo7EBDgrXFRxu0eWN9ZuwreCkhBgGR%2BeIIbaBQrdwy%2BokuDWHTmQ2KXSSO7%2Byn09rbgRucY39HgYXakggTjtnvhFD6nhKmDPrw%2Bk6vuFXHRWyoScfNyvtD7GuB%2Bq99mM1gcTfEslu7OfuOJOT3TW1sbzgi6yYyKXQupTFJgW7LJn45wceieqv%2BZzsqjeWi8Gl2zUucMZEPvKcUpO6tCYSUHdwuLpCTbRwWbmEUgomMmxSyIzlzpumX9kudnYPwhwUa0jBmKiSww%2BsgNsoOAIAAA%3D%3D" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Open in the playground</a></p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;script benchmark data-count="1000000"&gt;

const str = '+-111+++22-33*****4//////3';

// @benchmark Tim
function strip(s) {
    var out = "";
    var last = 'X';
    for( let i = 0; i &lt; s.length; i++ )
    {
        const c = s[i];
        if( "+-*/".indexOf(c) &lt; 0 || c != last )
        {
            out = out + c;
        }
        last = c;
    }
    return out;
}
//@run
strip(str)

// @benchmark regexp
str.replace(/([-/*+])\1+/g, '$1');

// @benchmark Array::reduce()
str.split('').reduce((r,c,i,arr) =&gt; i &amp;&amp; arr[i-1] === c &amp;&amp; '*/+-'.includes(c) ? r : r + c, '');

&lt;/script&gt;
&lt;script src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/silentmantra/benchmark/loader.js"&gt;&lt;/script&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>
